-- title:
--   Non-central approximable norm-one element at a place w ≠ v
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be negative rationals and let $O \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order, i.e. contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is finitely generated. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ contains an element that is non-zero and not a unit, and let $w \neq v$ be another height-one prime. Then there is $s \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ with $s \neq 1$ and $s \neq -1$ such that: (i) for every ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ onto $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w, a, b]$ (structure constants being the images of $a,b$) satisfying $\varphi(z \otimes r) = r \cdot (z_{\mathrm{re}}, z_{\mathrm{imI}}, z_{\mathrm{imJ}}, z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ coordinatewise, one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(s)) = x_0^2 - a x_1^2 - b x_2^2 + ab x_3^2 = 1$; and (ii) for every non-zero natural number $M$ there is $\beta \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta) = 1$ such that $\beta \otimes 1 \in 1 + M \cdot \mathrm{localBox}(O, w')$ for every height-one prime $w' \notin \{v,w\}$, and $\beta \otimes 1 \in s + M \cdot \mathrm{localBox}(O, w)$, where $\mathrm{localBox}(O,u)$ denotes the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_u$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_u$. The norm-one condition on $s$ in (i) is stated for all coordinate isomorphisms $\varphi$ of the indicated shape.
--
--   This is the local input to Kneser's proof of strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ relative to the set consisting of the archimedean place and $v$: at a place $w \neq v$ the closure of the congruence subgroups of the global norm-one elements is not central. It is used in the two statements producing a factorisation of a finite-idelic element of reduced norm one as a diagonal global element times a congruence element.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_ne_neg_one_forall_exists_nrd_eq_one_tmul_eq_add_smul.lean

